  "body": "## What changed\n\nThe tool editor shows the conservative parameter floor for an unchanged machine-default holder.\nThe displayed bands come from the stored profile and the editor's current tool dimensions.\nExplicit bodies and edited or imported drafts keep their own envelope.\n\n## Cause\n\nThe editor rebuilt every body from facets as an explicit preview.\nThat discarded machine-default provenance and omitted the parameter-cylinder floor used by collision checks.\nRebuilding facets also loses the stored profile's exact bands.\nThis change reads the stored profile for an unchanged default body and applies the existing floor rule.\nCollision and post behavior stay unchanged.\n\n## Tests\n\nSeven UI pins pass:\n\n- `machine_default_editor_envelope_matches_checked_parameter_floor`\n- `machine_default_editor_envelope_tracks_parameter_edits`\n- `explicit_editor_body_still_replaces_parameter_cylinder`\n- `moved_default_body_is_an_explicit_editor_draft`\n- `replaced_default_mesh_is_an_explicit_editor_draft`\n- `invalid_default_body_placement_has_no_editor_envelope`\n- `lathe_frame_default_body_has_no_spindle_editor_envelope`\n\nThe first two pins failed before the fix.\nRestoring upstream production code made both fail again.\nRestoring the fix passed all seven pins.\nRemoving each guard separately made its control fail.\nRestoring each guard made that control pass.\nThese mutations cover default provenance, facet identity, axis, offset, and lathe frame.\n\n`cargo xtask gate quick --base upstream/main` passed.\nThe UI library passed 822 tests with six ignored.\nThe boundary, boundary_picks, sinker_setup, and theme_files suites passed all 25 tests.\n`cargo clippy -p camcraft-ui --all-targets -- -D warnings` passed.\n\n## Goldens moved\n\nNone.\nThe NC and CL diff stat is empty.\n\n## Not exercised\n\nNo interactive desktop session, release pixel snapshots, or physical machining.\nThe before-and-after images below use the shipping tool editor in the headless egui renderer.\nThe pins exercise the envelope supplied to the editor painter.\n\n## Before and after\n\nThe same unchanged machine-default holder is shown in both images.\nThe tool has an 8 mm cutter, 20 mm flutes, a 40 mm shank, and a 60 mm diameter by 60 mm parameter holder.\nThe stored default body has radius 12 mm from 60 to 80 mm above the tip.\nBefore, the amber envelope covers only the narrow stored body.\nAfter, it also covers the conservative parameter-cylinder floor, radius 30 mm from 60 to 120 mm above the tip.\nThe fixture matches `machine_default_editor_envelope_matches_checked_parameter_floor`.\nThese are headless renders of the shipping tool editor, using the parent envelope function before and the fixed function after.\n\nBefore:\n\n![Before: amber envelope omits the wider parameter-cylinder floor](https://raw.githubusercontent.com/mkinney/Camcraft/e370f94f4353a7c1b38f18a4dd9769cb9a7d781c/2041/before.png)\n\nAfter:\n\n![After: amber envelope includes the wider parameter-cylinder floor](https://raw.githubusercontent.com/mkinney/Camcraft/e370f94f4353a7c1b38f18a4dd9769cb9a7d781c/2041/after.png)\n\n## Overlaps\n\nNone in the changed files.\nPR #2010 changes the downstream preview painter in `pages.rs` for #2005.\nThis PR changes `tool_body_page::envelope` and has no stacked dependency.\n\nEffort: medium.\nBased on upstream/main 2f6de7c5b, after v0.21.0.\nThe final gate used that merge base with upstream/main at 17a8c6e7608.\n\nChangelog: The tool editor shows the conservative parameter-cylinder floor of an unchanged machine-default holder.\n\nFixes #2009\n",
